 \$1+{\textbackslash}Omega(1) {\textbackslash}leq {\textbackslash}alpha {\textbackslash}leq O(1)\$, QSD\$\_\{{\textbackslash}alpha\}\$ is \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{BQP\}\$-complete. - For any \$1 {\textbackslash}leq {\textbackslash}alpha {\textbackslash}leq 1+{\textbackslash}frac\{1\}\{n\}\$, QSD\$\_\{{\textbackslash}alpha\}\$ is \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{QSZK\}\$-complete, implying that no efficient quantum estimator for \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{T\}\_{\textbackslash}alpha({\textbackslash}rho\_0,{\textbackslash}rho\_1)\$ exists unless \${\textbackslash}mathsf\{BQP\} = {\textbackslash}mathsf\{QSZK\}\$. The hardness results follow from reductions based on new rank-dependent inequalities for the quantum \${\textbackslash}ell\_\{{\textbackslash}alpha\}\$ distance with \$1{\textbackslash}leq {\textbackslash}alpha {\textbackslash}leq {\textbackslash}infty\$, which are of independent interest.},
