	abstract = {We give a construction of quantum LDPC codes of dimension \${\textbackslash}Theta({\textbackslash}log N)\$ and distance \${\textbackslash}Theta(N/{\textbackslash}log N)\$ as the code length \$N{\textbackslash}to{\textbackslash}infty\$. Using a product of chain complexes this construction also provides a family of quantum LDPC codes of distance \${\textbackslash}Omega(N{\textasciicircum}\{1-{\textbackslash}alpha/2\}/{\textbackslash}log N)\$ and dimension \${\textbackslash}Omega(N{\textasciicircum}{\textbackslash}alpha {\textbackslash}log N)\$, where \$0 {\textbackslash}le {\textbackslash}alpha {\textless} 1\$. We also introduce and study a new operation called lifted product, which naturally generalizes the product operations for quantum codes and chain complexes. Moreover, as a simple byproduct of our results on quantum codes, we obtain a new result on classical codes. We show that for any fixed \$R {\textless} 1\$ there exists an asymptotically good family of classical quasi-cyclic LDPC codes of rate at least \$R\$ with, in some sense, optimal circulant size \${\textbackslash}Omega(N/{\textbackslash}log N)\$ as the code length \$N{\textbackslash}to{\textbackslash}infty\$.},
