	abstract = {We present an object-oriented Python library for computation of properties of highly-excited Rydberg states of alkali atoms. These include single-body eﬀects such as dipole matrix elements, excited-state lifetimes (radiative and black-body limited) and Stark maps of atoms in external electric ﬁelds, as well as two-atom interaction potentials accounting for dipole and quadrupole coupling eﬀects valid at both long and short range for arbitrary placement of the atomic dipoles. The package is cross-referenced to precise measurements of atomic energy levels and features extensive documentation to facilitate rapid upgrade or expansion by users. This library has direct application in the ﬁeld of quantum information and quantum optics which exploit the strong Rydberg dipolar interactions for two-qubit gates, robust atom-light interfaces and simulating quantum many-body physics, as well as the ﬁeld of metrology using Rydberg atoms as precise microwave electrometers.},
