	title = {Universal fault-tolerant quantum computation with {Bacon}-{Shor} codes},
	url = {http://arxiv.org/abs/1705.01686},
	abstract = {We present a fault-tolerant universal gate set consisting of Hadamard and controlled-controlled-Z (CCZ) on Bacon-Shor subsystem codes. Transversal non-Clifford gates on these codes are intriguing in that higher levels of the Clifford hierarchy become accessible as the code becomes more asymmetric. For instance, in an appropriate gauge, Bacon-Shor codes on an \$m{\textbackslash}times m{\textasciicircum}k\$ lattice have transversal \$k\$-qubit-controlled \$Z\$. Through a variety of tricks, including intermediate error-correction and non-Pauli recovery, we reduce the overhead required for fault-tolerant CCZ. We calculate pseudothresholds for our universal gate set on the smallest \$3{\textbackslash}times3\$ Bacon-Shor code and also compare our gates with magic-states within the framework of a proposed ion trap architecture.},
